  "caveats": [
    "Filtering always reduces trade count; that is not a benefit. The filter earns its place only by RAISING alpha on what it keeps.",
    "Confirmed on futures, not options. The live filter reads an option's own premium, which decays; a future does not.",
    "Continuous futures are back-adjusted by the broker, which shifts levels. The ST trend state is shape-driven so it is largely preserved, but this is a real difference from the per-contract series the engine reads.",
    "Measures the UNDERLYING's move \u2014 an upper bound on a long-premium option position, never an estimate of one."
